# Coldline - Task 4.5
# File: .semgrepignore
# Component: Static-analysis scope
# Purpose: Keep Semgrep on the repository's own files: no tool caches, no virtual environment, no generated reports.
# Interacts With: poe security-scan, security/semgrep-rules.yaml
# Sprint/Task: Sprint 4 - Project 4 / Task 4.5
# Concepts: Scanning the files at the pull request's head, and nothing beside them
# Tools: Semgrep

# `poe security-scan` already hands Semgrep a copy of the tracked and untracked files that
# Git does not ignore, so these entries are a second guard, not the first. Every path the
# scanners read is listed here explicitly rather than left to Semgrep's defaults, which
# would also skip tests/ and are not pinned by this repository.
.git/
.venv/
.tools/
.mypy_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.semgrep_logs/
reports/
evidence/
